{"id": "clm:f7c50db9732198a1c5867e59df92221cdf78129ca0103afd985023f6036b0dc7", "type": "statement", "text": "The operation is not atomic, and MongoDB warns against running it in parallel with other key-management operations. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/method/KeyVault.rewrapManyDataKey.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Client-side encryption DEK rewrapping with rewrapManyDataKey"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "definition", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:8140553e8572ad798eff0b60826a4a371f35e1a77148158b3c1f2f088cca6c9e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:d6e2dd9f460a8ff24bc0d00a09f993c3e13628e15995b42f0432c571baffb804"]}
{"id": "clm:0aba896cc788fa5ea3d4937c39bb62002b2e831a2471f268fa21048caca7e38e", "type": "statement", "text": "The historical MONGOCRYPT-464 bug affected rewrapping with libmongocrypt 1.5.0/1.5.1: when Azure- or GCP-backed DEK decryption required fetching an access token, rewrapping could replace original key material with random material. The documented fix was libmongocrypt 1.5.2. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://jira.mongodb.org/browse/PHPC-2120", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Client-side encryption DEK rewrapping with rewrapManyDataKey"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "mechanism", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://github.com/mongodb/specifications/blob/master/source/client-side-encryption/client-side-encryption.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:8140553e8572ad798eff0b60826a4a371f35e1a77148158b3c1f2f088cca6c9e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:1c21b2393a68b8e57ca9cd1db013599ca3fbe92c49c29c788f1e5225a759da1b"]}
{"id": "clm:5ec305b76837a834abf56e1fe09afd57c11bfd24c450efb99ffa81844e7157d3", "type": "statement", "text": "The driver API returns RewrapManyDataKeyResult with an optional bulkWriteResult; it can be absent when no keys match or when the bulk write is unacknowledged. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://github.com/mongodb/specifications/blob/master/source/client-side-encryption/client-side-encryption.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Client-side encryption DEK rewrapping with rewrapManyDataKey"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "mechanism", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:8140553e8572ad798eff0b60826a4a371f35e1a77148158b3c1f2f088cca6c9e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:1e3e81792440da1389cfb95356bd0fbf706a3fb66f88ac35139a6d8ff24f1d16"]}
{"id": "clm:857a878b7cc38c10a05cc4240b6a8d9220c2350ebe0c9bef7769f1fab1c6b4f8", "type": "statement", "text": "The options identify the target KMS provider and provider-specific masterKey. When masterKey is omitted, each DEK uses the CMK referenced in its existing metadata. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/method/KeyVault.rewrapManyDataKey.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Client-side encryption DEK rewrapping with rewrapManyDataKey"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "mechanism", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/core/queryable-encryption/fundamentals/manage-keys.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:8140553e8572ad798eff0b60826a4a371f35e1a77148158b3c1f2f088cca6c9e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:977f896e80fafd9bb1637b9b230fbbfe684572318fcba448a18736b11443bcfa"]}
{"id": "clm:0ea2a9a80e1beaa2380fee20c640a49fd0d758174e0768c86777ac7d6ea485de", "type": "statement", "text": "AWS KMS key-material rotation preserves the logical KMS key and selects the original key material when decrypting existing ciphertext. It does not rotate data keys or mitigate a compromised data key; MongoDB likewise leaves DEK material unchanged when rewrapping. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/rotate-keys.html", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Client-side encryption DEK rewrapping with rewrapManyDataKey"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "mechanism", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/core/queryable-encryption/fundamentals/keys-key-vaults.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:8140553e8572ad798eff0b60826a4a371f35e1a77148158b3c1f2f088cca6c9e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:005b68f96190220550109121f580761154fabe0d5760387786f16f22603cd9a7", "ev:cc4cfc4b4b07be0c088cea41bf28765a1e04114f5adeb8edaf0f74e2db29902b"]}
{"id": "clm:2165f01c02259701819e88a06f6d0b2e7550f9a9851f1edca20f353cb608538b", "type": "statement", "text": "rewrapManyDataKey decrypts existing DEKs and re-encrypts their unchanged plaintext key material under the selected CMK. Rewrapping changes key protection rather than replacing the DEKs that encrypt application fields. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/core/queryable-encryption/fundamentals/keys-key-vaults.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Client-side encryption DEK rewrapping with rewrapManyDataKey"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "comparisons", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/method/KeyVault.rewrapManyDataKey.md", "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/core/queryable-encryption/fundamentals/manage-keys.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:8140553e8572ad798eff0b60826a4a371f35e1a77148158b3c1f2f088cca6c9e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:60ab4d7a1d42dc4181f5f09092a9c22b43ce6390ae9f7d90d5874dd03ddca6f3", "ev:d3241134fbd00b3bd0c1a476efdf50ea17fddd81ae3bd370d1c67b0445c76f09"]}
{"id": "clm:39addd5c883e78a3e25b62ad0876e0f49d39ddc505699eb0641cf029a617f321", "type": "statement", "text": "The key vault stores CMK-encrypted DEKs. A client needs both key-vault access and access to the protecting KMS key to use a DEK; the key vault can reside on a separate MongoDB cluster. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/core/queryable-encryption/fundamentals/keys-key-vaults.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Client-side encryption DEK rewrapping with rewrapManyDataKey"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://github.com/mongodb/specifications/blob/master/source/client-side-encryption/client-side-encryption.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:8140553e8572ad798eff0b60826a4a371f35e1a77148158b3c1f2f088cca6c9e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:f5c3eaacf8d7c1987285451695e010dd46e45f41b710f991d5aa1eee4f670bb8"]}
{"id": "clm:ba4ab2ebdfac2215868a41ff6716db0ea220ece0c519af7bfd3e8045edf1092e", "type": "statement", "text": "Rotating the KMS key does not itself rewrap existing stored DEKs. AWS additionally documents that key rotation does not replace data keys, re-encrypt protected data, or mitigate a compromised data key. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/core/queryable-encryption/fundamentals/keys-key-vaults.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Client-side encryption DEK rewrapping with rewrapManyDataKey"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/rotate-keys.html"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:8140553e8572ad798eff0b60826a4a371f35e1a77148158b3c1f2f088cca6c9e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:005b68f96190220550109121f580761154fabe0d5760387786f16f22603cd9a7", "ev:cc4cfc4b4b07be0c088cea41bf28765a1e04114f5adeb8edaf0f74e2db29902b"]}
{"id": "clm:b654fa0e854eae474e42cd62f3f7c07ccb914845f3fb82871fe235ec9231aafc", "type": "statement", "text": "The filter selects key-vault documents to rewrap. If no key matches, the driver performs no bulk write; without a new masterKey, DEKs are rewrapped using their current master keys. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/method/KeyVault.rewrapManyDataKey.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Client-side encryption DEK rewrapping with rewrapManyDataKey"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://github.com/mongodb/specifications/blob/master/source/client-side-encryption/client-side-encryption.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:8140553e8572ad798eff0b60826a4a371f35e1a77148158b3c1f2f088cca6c9e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:a0de1427615548bbbe6b37145b5fbe97c89f0e5fb8747e968b2c0b9491d94514"]}
{"id": "clm:c9558aa1c8dacb22596742155151cd5f2914788f827c5498e58b4928e8dd2737", "type": "statement", "text": "Back up the key-vault collection before rewrapping: losing DEK material can make the corresponding encrypted data unrecoverable. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/method/KeyVault.rewrapManyDataKey.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Client-side encryption DEK rewrapping with rewrapManyDataKey"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://jira.mongodb.org/browse/PHPC-2120"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:8140553e8572ad798eff0b60826a4a371f35e1a77148158b3c1f2f088cca6c9e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:f5d1e12cb654ac425f83a7eeec87622525ed02d2d7b303a00ce06b464c8ae1ac"]}
{"id": "clm:8c4440b080e0081bcdf2e69af087f90eee5b665bc61dcfee430ef091b3963a1e", "type": "statement", "text": "The client-side encryption specification requires applicable drivers to reject rewrapManyDataKey with libmongocrypt 1.5.0 or 1.5.1 and document dependency upgrades for MONGOCRYPT-464. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://github.com/mongodb/specifications/blob/master/source/client-side-encryption/client-side-encryption.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Client-side encryption DEK rewrapping with rewrapManyDataKey"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:8140553e8572ad798eff0b60826a4a371f35e1a77148158b3c1f2f088cca6c9e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:343f9b265d7933e270cf02fad816302d5750906758b1513950ea2f1733ca4e8b"]}
{"id": "clm:ee539d38cf3401f99a9295eef937870222baf6378c722e7774f8b796d603348b", "type": "statement", "text": "Fortanix documents a concrete KMIP integration sequence: rotate the CMK in DSM, then call ClientEncryption.rewrapManyDataKey with the returned CMK identifier as masterKey.keyId and the chosen provider. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://support.fortanix.com/v1/docs/fortanix-dsm-for-mongodb-client-side-field-level-encryption", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Client-side encryption DEK rewrapping with rewrapManyDataKey"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:8140553e8572ad798eff0b60826a4a371f35e1a77148158b3c1f2f088cca6c9e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:caca2108a7dedfa67b4fc8e53a0ab674fb2cf5367810d05a34edb27145fda348"]}
{"id": "clm:b5fcdd71b91d8daf20015af7ce212d5a65a9b0ecf41605b7979d557e8e834dd1", "type": "statement", "text": "rewrapManyDataKey decrypts matching wrapped DEKs, re-encrypts them under a specified CMK, and updates their documents in the Key Vault collection. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/method/KeyVault.rewrapManyDataKey.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Client-side encryption DEK rewrapping with rewrapManyDataKey"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/core/queryable-encryption/fundamentals/manage-keys.md", "https://support.fortanix.com/v1/docs/fortanix-dsm-for-mongodb-client-side-field-level-encryption"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:8140553e8572ad798eff0b60826a4a371f35e1a77148158b3c1f2f088cca6c9e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:60ab4d7a1d42dc4181f5f09092a9c22b43ce6390ae9f7d90d5874dd03ddca6f3"]}
{"id": "clm:2bbdefb1b0dcd03588cb2be23177d035f5d770c52d4017857fd9fbe4af75e20b", "type": "statement", "text": "Rotating a CMK at the KMS does not automatically rewrap existing MongoDB DEKs; an explicit rewrapManyDataKey operation performs that separate step. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/core/queryable-encryption/fundamentals/keys-key-vaults.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Client-side encryption DEK rewrapping with rewrapManyDataKey"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/core/queryable-encryption/fundamentals/manage-keys.md", "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/rotate-keys.html"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:8140553e8572ad798eff0b60826a4a371f35e1a77148158b3c1f2f088cca6c9e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:005b68f96190220550109121f580761154fabe0d5760387786f16f22603cd9a7"]}
{"id": "clm:3f5895931b184ab9ddf4d13f7ed2167f9f62a95a941d97a6a5b26276220ee844", "type": "statement", "text": "The query filter selects Key Vault documents to rewrap; an empty filter selects all keys. If no keys match, the driver specification requires no bulk write and leaves bulkWriteResult unset. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/core/queryable-encryption/fundamentals/manage-keys.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Client-side encryption DEK rewrapping with rewrapManyDataKey"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://github.com/mongodb/specifications/blob/master/source/client-side-encryption/client-side-encryption.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:8140553e8572ad798eff0b60826a4a371f35e1a77148158b3c1f2f088cca6c9e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:1e3e81792440da1389cfb95356bd0fbf706a3fb66f88ac35139a6d8ff24f1d16", "ev:60ab4d7a1d42dc4181f5f09092a9c22b43ce6390ae9f7d90d5874dd03ddca6f3", "ev:a0de1427615548bbbe6b37145b5fbe97c89f0e5fb8747e968b2c0b9491d94514"]}
{"id": "clm:45bb57f806731af56180acff5821f3432217344e639b5265aac46c4e66014880", "type": "statement", "text": "Back up the Key Vault before rewrapping and confirm that keys no longer protect any required data or keys before deleting them. Losing a required DEK or CMK can make encrypted fields permanently unreadable. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/method/KeyVault.rewrapManyDataKey.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Client-side encryption DEK rewrapping with rewrapManyDataKey"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/core/queryable-encryption/fundamentals/manage-keys.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:8140553e8572ad798eff0b60826a4a371f35e1a77148158b3c1f2f088cca6c9e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:b13896130bcf026889b1792bcf2122ae3a72859eb13deb1ef06042c46c215e3a", "ev:f5d1e12cb654ac425f83a7eeec87622525ed02d2d7b303a00ce06b464c8ae1ac"]}
{"id": "clm:716c9c75a6bd8a649e7dfba99f85df3e59d94e707df3268afb54b8aa34ffa85c", "type": "statement", "text": "MongoDB's mongosh v1.5.4 release notes, dated July 31, 2022, describe a destructive historical bug: rewrapping an Azure- or GCP-backed DEK that required fetching an access token for decryption could replace all rewrapped DEKs with random material. The release notes identify v1.5.4 as the shell fix. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/mongodb-shell/changelog.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Client-side encryption DEK rewrapping with rewrapManyDataKey"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:8140553e8572ad798eff0b60826a4a371f35e1a77148158b3c1f2f088cca6c9e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:7a2e2b58e7c17f4bdb73061190466064754444d639b7d7669d026c42b43d7412"]}
